#{[{:activity/course {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186046660} :activity/first-step {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186549138} :activity/id #uuid "ecdaae25-bed5-51c6-92d7-0d48e0fe1dcc" :activity/scope {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050993 :topic/id #uuid "77b8e530-6866-509a-8397-d35f1b4f5874" :topic/math-academy-id 2097} :activity/steps [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186549116 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186360772 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ac261e67-ef83-599b-9f7a-2f0221d53c55" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452335} {:answer/id #uuid "a8955430-a9ed-5bcb-ac12-138c73b1312a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452336}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186452335} :answer-field/id #uuid "26ce4c66-39b4-5114-9f3a-f7a49fb4749a" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453015} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c4385f63-a19e-59b3-b375-1f827b7a2b42" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452337} {:answer/id #uuid "f93fb5fe-2a57-5b9f-8207-21687f865974" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452338}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186452338} :answer-field/id #uuid "6e2913a5-5b90-507c-ba81-c9f768ab74f3" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453016} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b1d2b1a3-de50-5a4d-8436-402d7d7ff9e1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452339} {:answer/id #uuid "80eb1877-a06a-52e2-9a0b-c6ad7075ac0e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452340}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186452339} :answer-field/id #uuid "efec9971-12d9-5dac-9de5-e52ca41b457f" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453017}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "ea5645c8-5c4c-53e6-a126-c5a12be2f712" :question/math-academy-id "q-97229" :question/problem "Consider the standard Hermitian inner product $⟨\\,\\cdot \\,,\\,\\cdot \\,⟩$ over $C.$ \nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $⟨a,b⟩=⟨b,a⟩$ for any $a,b\\in {C}^{n}$\n- **II.** $⟨ia,ia⟩=⟨a,a⟩$ for any $a\\in {C}^{n}$\n- **III.** $⟨a,b⟩\\in R$ for any $a,b\\in {C}^{n}$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that the standard Hermitian inner product over $C$ satisfies the following properties:\n\n- It is linear in the first argument. For any $a,b,c\\in {C}^{n}$ and any $\\alpha \\in C,$ we have\n\n$\\,$ $⟨a+b,c⟩=⟨a,c⟩+⟨b,c⟩\\,$ and $\\,⟨\\alpha a,b⟩=\\alpha ⟨a,b⟩.$\n\n- It is antilinear in the second argument. For any $a,b,c\\in {C}^{n}$ and any $\\alpha \\in C,$ we have\n\n$\\,$ $⟨a,b+c⟩=⟨a,b⟩+⟨a,c⟩\\,$ and $\\,⟨a,\\alpha b⟩=\\overset{―}{\\alpha }⟨a,b⟩.$\n\n- It has conjugate symmetry. For any $a,b\\in {C}^{n},$ we have\n\n$\\,$ $⟨a,b⟩=\\overset{―}{⟨b,a⟩}.$\n\n- It is positive-definite. For any $a\\in {C}^{n},$ we have\n\n$\\,$ $⟨a,a⟩$ is a non-negative real number, and $⟨a,a⟩=0$ if and only if $a=0.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our statements.\n\n- Statement I is false. The inner product over $C$ has conjugate symmetry.\n\n- Statement II is true. Indeed, by the linearity in the first argument  and the antilinearity in the second argument we have\n\n$$\n⟨ia,ia⟩=(i\\cdot \\overset{¯}{i})⟨a,a⟩=-{i}^{2}⟨a,a⟩=⟨a,a⟩.\n$$\n\n- Statement III is false. The inner product over $C$ is a complex number, in general.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only.\""} :step/id #uuid "809a8a72-7832-5099-b9a5-45e402cf6e7f" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186549155}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186549128 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186360765 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5c87f659-1f7f-5209-836f-e2358c8758ed" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-5-3\\text{i}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186358558} {:answer/id #uuid "c588ae26-6ffe-5a64-9cd1-d99c48a22af7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-3+2\\text{i}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186359483} {:answer/id #uuid "cb41abdd-b96d-59b4-80a5-e1d5e4813b07" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "8+3\\text{i}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186359536} {:answer/id #uuid "e1814899-f61e-5394-8d34-d1ef3abb1571" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186359743} {:answer/id #uuid "ee7c4496-6fc8-56cb-b338-f96b969713ff" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "8\\text{i}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186359877}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186359536} :answer-field/id #uuid "dbef6978-7d21-5038-b288-d6341fb0e7c9" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186360384}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "926d966b-0333-5eff-ad69-722d66b05ff2" :question/math-academy-id "q-97180" :question/problem "Given that $⟨\\,\\cdot \\,,\\,\\cdot \\,⟩$ is the standard Hermitian inner product over $C,$ find $⟨a,\\,b+(2+5\\text{i})c⟩$ if \n\n$\\,$ $⟨b,a⟩=3-\\text{i}\\,$ and $\\,⟨a,c⟩=\\text{i}.$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that the inner product over $C$ satisfies the following properties. \n\n- It is linear in the first argument. For any $a,b,c\\in {C}^{n}$ and any $\\alpha \\in C,$ we have\n\n$\\,$ $⟨a+b,c⟩=⟨a,c⟩+⟨b,c⟩\\,$ and $\\,⟨\\alpha a,b⟩=\\alpha ⟨a,b⟩.$\n\n- It is antilinear in the second argument. For any $a,b,c\\in {C}^{n}$ and any $\\alpha \\in C,$ we have\n\n$\\,$ $⟨a,b+c⟩=⟨a,b⟩+⟨a,c⟩\\,$ and $\\,⟨a,\\alpha b⟩=\\overset{―}{\\alpha }⟨a,b⟩.$\n\n- It has conjugate symmetry. For any $a,b\\in {C}^{n},$ we have\n\n$\\,$ $⟨a,b⟩=\\overset{―}{⟨b,a⟩}.$\n\n- It is positive-definite. For any $a\\in {C}^{n},$ we have\n\n$\\,$ $⟨a,a⟩$ is a non-negative real number, and $⟨a,a⟩=0$ if and only if $a=0.$\n\nFirst, we use the fact that the inner product over $C$ is antilinear in the second argument:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨a,\\,b+(2+5\\text{i})c⟩ & =⟨a,b⟩+⟨a,(2+5\\text{i})c⟩ \\\\  & =⟨a,b⟩+(\\overset{―}{2+5\\text{i}})⟨a,c⟩ \\\\  & =⟨a,b⟩+(2-5\\text{i})⟨a,c⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we use the fact that the inner product over $C$ has conjugate symmetry:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨a,b⟩+(2-5\\text{i})⟨a,c⟩ & =\\overset{―}{⟨b,a⟩}+(2-5\\text{i})⟨a,c⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we substitute the values for $⟨b,a⟩$ and $⟨a,c⟩:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{―}{⟨b,a⟩}+(2-5\\text{i})⟨a,c⟩ & =\\overset{―}{3-\\text{i}}+(2-5\\text{i})\\cdot \\text{i} \\\\  & =3+\\text{i}+(2-5\\text{i})\\cdot \\text{i} \\\\  & =3+\\text{i}+2\\text{i}-5(-1) \\\\  & =8+3\\text{i}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "992c56a5-6fe0-5dc6-9f17-8ab4003e66fd" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186549147}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186549138 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186360761 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "53d42ef8-112a-540f-b044-e82877763aaa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "7-\\text{i}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186358478} {:answer/id #uuid "575188ec-dee7-52bc-98d2-b0c23f062037" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-5+7\\text{i}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186358510} {:answer/id #uuid "5c7b5a87-1155-5b0f-a42c-2a6730360e40" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "3-5\\text{i}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186358556} {:answer/id #uuid "767f4994-0324-5e33-9d63-bc6eb2a02ba7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-1+8\\text{i}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186358773} {:answer/id #uuid "e10a1386-5944-5e40-a9ab-897daed63700" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "15-10\\text{i}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186359736}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186359736} :answer-field/id #uuid "805db896-5b3b-5974-b4ac-1d6fe4b7b00a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186360208}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "e5cc7f04-77b2-544c-b6f7-4b258e1d90be" :question/math-academy-id "q-97159" :question/problem "Given that $⟨\\,\\cdot \\,,\\,\\cdot \\,⟩$ is the standard Hermitian inner product over $C,$ find $⟨a,\\,6b+c⟩$ if   \n\n$\\,$ $⟨b,a⟩=2+3\\text{i}\\,$ and $\\,⟨a,c⟩=3+8\\text{i}.$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that the inner product over $C$ satisfies the following properties. \n\n- It is linear in the first argument. For any $a,b,c\\in {C}^{n}$ and any $\\alpha \\in C,$ we have\n\n$\\,$ $⟨a+b,c⟩=⟨a,c⟩+⟨b,c⟩\\,$ and $\\,⟨\\alpha a,b⟩=\\alpha ⟨a,b⟩.$\n\n- It is antilinear in the second argument. For any $a,b,c\\in {C}^{n}$ and any $\\alpha \\in C,$ we have\n\n$\\,$ $⟨a,b+c⟩=⟨a,b⟩+⟨a,c⟩\\,$ and $\\,⟨a,\\alpha b⟩=\\overset{―}{\\alpha }⟨a,b⟩.$\n\n- It has conjugate symmetry. For any $a,b\\in {C}^{n},$ we have\n\n$\\,$ $⟨a,b⟩=\\overset{―}{⟨b,a⟩}.$\n\n- It is positive-definite. For any $a\\in {C}^{n},$ we have\n\n$\\,$ $⟨a,a⟩$ is a non-negative real number, and $⟨a,a⟩=0$ if and only if $a=0.$\n\nFirst, we use the fact that the inner product over $C$ is antilinear in the second argument:  \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨a,\\,6b+c⟩ & =⟨a,6b⟩+⟨a,c⟩ \\\\  & =\\overset{―}{6}⟨a,b⟩+⟨a,c⟩ \\\\  & =6⟨a,b⟩+⟨a,c⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n  \n\nNext, we use the fact that the inner product over $C$ has conjugate symmetry: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}6⟨a,b⟩+⟨a,c⟩ & =6\\overset{―}{⟨b,a⟩}+⟨a,c⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we substitute the values for $⟨b,a⟩$ and $⟨a,c⟩:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}6\\overset{―}{⟨b,a⟩}+⟨a,c⟩ & =6(\\overset{―}{2+3\\text{i}})+(3+8\\text{i}) \\\\  & =6(2-3\\text{i})+(3+8\\text{i}) \\\\  & =12-18\\text{i}+3+8\\text{i} \\\\  & =15-10\\text{i}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "be0276ea-a708-51f8-888a-7f3184b163e3" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186549128}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186549147 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186360767 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0e841129-5370-59a4-a247-981a63a55e7e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186357872} {:answer/id #uuid "0f6fe134-1090-5f97-9ea8-128ddfc3b774" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-\\text{i}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186357876} {:answer/id #uuid "c020effb-ac1b-5c1a-b136-a3f990641cda" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-2\\text{i}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186359435} {:answer/id #uuid "cb7d8484-175b-5e8d-bc3b-f162579d8e47" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "3\\text{i}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186359541} {:answer/id #uuid "e819a706-cc55-53d4-ad1b-913fba1a9b02" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-5+3\\text{i}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186359809}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186359541} :answer-field/id #uuid "a14982e8-8062-5f22-9abd-32b12535e617" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186360273}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "34140471-4f5c-5a2d-9e46-e76840a3d73f" :question/math-academy-id "q-97193" :question/problem "Given that $⟨\\,\\cdot \\,,\\,\\cdot \\,⟩$ is the standard Hermitian inner product over $C,$ find $⟨a,\\,(4-\\text{i})b+c⟩$ if  \n\n$\\,$ $⟨b,a⟩=-1-\\text{i}\\,$ and $\\,⟨a,c⟩=5.$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that the inner product over $C$ satisfies the following properties. \n\n- It is linear in the first argument. For any $a,b,c\\in {C}^{n}$ and any $\\alpha \\in C,$ we have\n\n$\\,$ $⟨a+b,c⟩=⟨a,c⟩+⟨b,c⟩\\,$ and $\\,⟨\\alpha a,b⟩=\\alpha ⟨a,b⟩.$\n\n- It is antilinear in the second argument. For any $a,b,c\\in {C}^{n}$ and any $\\alpha \\in C,$ we have\n\n$\\,$ $⟨a,b+c⟩=⟨a,b⟩+⟨a,c⟩\\,$ and $\\,⟨a,\\alpha b⟩=\\overset{―}{\\alpha }⟨a,b⟩.$\n\n- It has conjugate symmetry. For any $a,b\\in {C}^{n},$ we have\n\n$\\,$ $⟨a,b⟩=\\overset{―}{⟨b,a⟩}.$\n\n- It is positive-definite. For any $a\\in {C}^{n},$ we have\n\n$\\,$ $⟨a,a⟩$ is a non-negative real number, and $⟨a,a⟩=0$ if and only if $a=0.$\n\nFirst, we use the fact that the inner product over $C$ is antilinear in the second argument:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨a,\\,(4-\\text{i})b+c⟩ & =⟨a,(4-\\text{i})b⟩+⟨a,c⟩ \\\\  & =(\\overset{―}{4-\\text{i}})⟨a,b⟩+⟨a,c⟩ \\\\  & =(4+\\text{i})⟨a,b⟩+⟨a,c⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we use the fact that the inner product over $C$ has conjugate symmetry:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(4+\\text{i})⟨a,b⟩+⟨a,c\\text{ }⟩ & =(4+\\text{i})\\overset{―}{⟨b,a⟩}+⟨a,c⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we substitute the values for $⟨b,a⟩$ and $⟨a,c⟩:$  \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(4+\\text{i})\\overset{―}{⟨b,a⟩}+⟨a,c⟩ & =(4+\\text{i})\\cdot (\\overset{―}{-1-\\text{i}})+5 \\\\  & =(4+\\text{i})\\cdot (-1+\\text{i})+5 \\\\  & =-5+3\\text{i}+5 \\\\  & =3\\text{i}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "db72b08f-87f9-553e-856e-a5aedbbe304d" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186549116}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186549155 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186272226 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9b355e36-38c2-56ac-8348-b3784bc1866b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449616} {:answer/id #uuid "b5f4aaaf-dd54-51ec-8f46-f6472f61e6a2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449617}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186449616} :answer-field/id #uuid "7641d15d-e8d6-5db7-b7ee-7fbcf01436a4" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450762} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9596a264-1604-5e56-9101-1d727a10926f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449618} {:answer/id #uuid "281f3fd1-7ba1-527c-ae04-c2bd6defe1dc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449619}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186449619} :answer-field/id #uuid "0b2f83df-bcf3-5451-9968-beb33cc6fea5" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450763} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "80cfc54f-6519-5a2f-8498-b86f5f3b2228" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449620} {:answer/id #uuid "f6e29156-a774-5d52-acbb-563e0b03f2a1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449621}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186449620} :answer-field/id #uuid "506b6c64-848b-5d2a-a9d9-9c59b4dab9a9" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450764}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "525bde81-7550-5f13-8e28-5c16a04ee9f0" :question/math-academy-id "q-141159" :question/problem "Consider the standard Hermitian inner product $⟨\\,\\cdot \\,,\\,\\cdot \\,⟩$ over $C.$ \nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $⟨a,b⟩=⟨b,a⟩$ for any $a,b\\in {C}^{n}$\n- **II.** $⟨a,\\alpha b⟩=\\alpha ⟨a,b⟩$ for any $a,b\\in {C}^{n}$ and any $\\alpha \\in R$\n- **III.** $⟨a,a⟩>0$ for any $a\\in {C}^{n}$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that the standard Hermitian inner product over $C$ satisfies the following properties:\n\n- It is linear in the first argument. For any $a,b,c\\in {C}^{n}$ and any $\\alpha \\in C,$ we have\n\n$\\,$ $⟨a+b,c⟩=⟨a,c⟩+⟨b,c⟩\\,$ and $\\,⟨\\alpha a,b⟩=\\alpha ⟨a,b⟩.$\n\n- It is antilinear in the second argument. For any $a,b,c\\in {C}^{n}$ and any $\\alpha \\in C,$ we have\n\n$\\,$ $⟨a,b+c⟩=⟨a,b⟩+⟨a,c⟩\\,$ and $\\,⟨a,\\alpha b⟩=\\overset{―}{\\alpha }⟨a,b⟩.$\n\n- It has conjugate symmetry. For any $a,b\\in {C}^{n},$ we have\n\n$\\,$ $⟨a,b⟩=\\overset{―}{⟨b,a⟩}.$\n\n- It is positive-definite. For any $a\\in {C}^{n},$ we have\n\n$\\,$ $⟨a,a⟩$ is a non-negative real number, and $⟨a,a⟩=0$ if and only if $a=0.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our statements.\n\n- Statement I is false. The inner product over $C$ has conjugate symmetry.\n\n- Statement II is true. For any $\\alpha \\in R,$ we have $\\overset{―}{\\alpha }=\\alpha .$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n⟨a,\\alpha b⟩=\\overset{―}{\\alpha }⟨a,b⟩=\\alpha ⟨a,b⟩.\n$$\n\n- Statement III is false. Notice that if $a=0,$ then $⟨a,a⟩=0.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only.\""} :step/id #uuid "fa4febc8-0ca9-5520-8222-9d6a4ac0440b"}] :activity/title "The Inner Product in Vector Spaces Over the Complex Numbers" :activity/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :activity.type/review} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186548355}]}
